      <p class="reality-check-description">
        If you're spending 3 hours a day in a college bus, that's 15
                  hours a week gone. In 4 years, that's over 2,000 hours you
                  could have used to master a skill. Choose a college with a
                  shorter commute or better hostel life over a "slightly better"
                  brand name far away.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="reality-check-card">
    <div class="reality-check-num">04</div>
    <div class="reality-check-content">
      <h3 class="reality-check-title">The Lab &amp; Wi-Fi Reality</h3>
      <p class="reality-check-description">
        During your visit, don't look at the gardens. Look at the
                  labs. Are the computers running Windows 7? Is the Wi-Fi
                  restricted? If you can't access high-speed internet or modern
                  hardware on campus, you're paying for an outdated education.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="reality-check-card">
    <div class="reality-check-num">05</div>
